{"post_stream":{"posts":[{"id":495180,"name":"Sanghoon Kang","username":"Sanghoon_Kang","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/sanghoon_kang/{size}/121272_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-18T15:55:51.771Z","cooked":"\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-495180-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-495180-where-does-the-bug-appear-featureproduct-1\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eWhere does the bug appear (feature/product)?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eGrok Bot\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-495180-describe-the-bug-2\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-495180-describe-the-bug-2\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDescribe the Bug\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHi Cursor team,\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’m opening this as a separate bug report following Colin’s suggestion in my previous Grok Bot thread.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSince yesterday, my Grok Bot has been unable to launch a delegated Cloud Agent because of the following error:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eResourceExhausted — vttablet transaction pool connection limit exceeded\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLatest Caller ID:\u003cbr\u003e\njqftxh24a9mn90ceno1y\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis does not appear to be my plan usage limit.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI upgraded to Cursor Ultra ($200/month), and my current usage is still very low:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCursor Models: ~6% used\u003cbr\u003e\nOther Models: ~1% used\u003cbr\u003e\nGrok Bot weekly usage: ~5%\u003cbr\u003e\nOn-demand spending: disabled\u003cbr\u003e\nThe workflow itself is ready and authorized, but the Cloud Agent cannot launch. We have retried at widely separated times, including again today, and the same ResourceExhausted / vttablet transaction pool error persists.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe parent/Builder correctly stops retrying and reports the task as PLATFORM BLOCKED, so there have been no repository changes or repeated retry loops.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCould you please confirm whether this is:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003ea Cursor-side Cloud Agent infrastructure/capacity issue,\u003cbr\u003e\nan account/workspace concurrency or connection-pool limit,\u003cbr\u003e\nor another Cloud Agent quota/limit that is separate from the Ultra usage shown in Plan \u0026amp; Usage?\u003cbr\u003e\nIf there is a way to inspect or reset the relevant Cloud Agent transaction pool for my account/workspace, that would also be very helpful.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe important distinction for me is whether I should simply wait for platform capacity to recover, or whether there is an account/workspace condition that needs intervention.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks!\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-495180-steps-to-reproduce-3\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-495180-steps-to-reproduce-3\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eSteps to Reproduce\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eOpen Grok Bot and use a parent/orchestrator Bot that delegates an implementation task to a project Builder Bot.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eHave the Builder launch a delegated Cursor Cloud Agent for an authorized implementation task.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Cloud Agent launch fails with:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eResourceExhausted — vttablet transaction pool connection limit exceeded\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col start=\"4\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eWait and retry later using the same authorized task. The same ResourceExhausted error occurs again.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIn my case this has persisted across widely separated attempts since the previous day, not just rapid consecutive retries.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eVerify Plan \u0026amp; Usage. My account is on Cursor Ultra ($200/month) and usage is far below the included limits:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCursor Models: approximately 6% used\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOther Models: approximately 1% used\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGrok Bot weekly usage: approximately 5%\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOn-demand spending: disabled\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003col start=\"7\"\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eThe Builder therefore cannot launch the Cloud Agent and correctly stops without modifying the repository.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLatest error:\u003cbr\u003e\nResourceExhausted — vttablet transaction pool connection limit exceeded\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLatest Caller ID:\u003cbr\u003e\njqftxh24a9mn90ceno1y\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-495180-expected-behavior-4\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-495180-expected-behavior-4\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eExpected Behavior\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eA delegated Cloud Agent should launch normally while the account has available included Ultra usage and there is no product/workflow authorization blocker.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf the Cloud Agent cannot launch because of a separate infrastructure, concurrency, transaction-pool, or account/workspace limit, the product should clearly identify that condition and distinguish it from normal plan usage exhaustion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf this is a temporary Cursor-side capacity issue, the launch should succeed once capacity is available again.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf there is an account/workspace-specific Cloud Agent connection or transaction-pool limit, the UI should expose the relevant limit/status or provide a clear recovery path.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-495180-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-495180-screenshots-screen-recordings-5\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eScreenshots / Screen Recordings\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/9/d/9d70490777cc9eb37cd6aee376a1a8f2b86234b7.png\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/msLx2D69dLXNnuTJvdmn0ZVjnqT.png?dl=1\" title=\"5997061d2f64c27790cf3ab3ce56fc818bf64914_2_1010x998.png\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/9/d/9d70490777cc9eb37cd6aee376a1a8f2b86234b7_2_506x499.png\" alt=\"5997061d2f64c27790cf3ab3ce56fc818bf64914_2_1010x998.png\" data-base62-sha1=\"msLx2D69dLXNnuTJvdmn0ZVjnqT\" width=\"506\" height=\"499\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/9/d/9d70490777cc9eb37cd6aee376a1a8f2b86234b7_2_506x499.png, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/9/d/9d70490777cc9eb37cd6aee376a1a8f2b86234b7_2_759x748.png 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/9/d/9d70490777cc9eb37cd6aee376a1a8f2b86234b7.png 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"F3F3F3\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003e5997061d2f64c27790cf3ab3ce56fc818bf64914_2_1010x998.png\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1010×998 54.3 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"lightbox-wrapper\"\u003e\u003ca class=\"lightbox\" href=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/0/b/0b1b6309d2fbb74972a2b1183b23b27a7c75abe6.jpeg\" data-download-href=\"/uploads/short-url/1AfVygPDE7t3ZkSgQ9XWETPT5tQ.jpeg?dl=1\" title=\"f5cdc5fde9137c5fbd17935561dcb519e7bdc604_2_1380x864.jpg\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\"\u003e\u003cimg src=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/0/b/0b1b6309d2fbb74972a2b1183b23b27a7c75abe6_2_690x432.jpeg\" alt=\"f5cdc5fde9137c5fbd17935561dcb519e7bdc604_2_1380x864.jpg\" data-base62-sha1=\"1AfVygPDE7t3ZkSgQ9XWETPT5tQ\" width=\"690\" height=\"432\" srcset=\"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/0/b/0b1b6309d2fbb74972a2b1183b23b27a7c75abe6_2_690x432.jpeg, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/0/b/0b1b6309d2fbb74972a2b1183b23b27a7c75abe6_2_1035x648.jpeg 1.5x, https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/optimized/3X/0/b/0b1b6309d2fbb74972a2b1183b23b27a7c75abe6_2_1380x864.jpeg 2x\" data-dominant-color=\"F1F1F0\"\u003e\u003cdiv class=\"meta\"\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-far-image svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#far-image\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003cspan class=\"filename\"\u003ef5cdc5fde9137c5fbd17935561dcb519e7bdc604_2_1380x864.jpg\u003c/span\u003e\u003cspan class=\"informations\"\u003e1380×864 92.7 KB\u003c/span\u003e\u003csvg class=\"fa d-icon d-icon-discourse-expand svg-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\"\u003e\u003cuse href=\"#discourse-expand\"\u003e\u003c/use\u003e\u003c/svg\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/div\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-495180-operating-system-6\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-495180-operating-system-6\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eOperating System\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eMacOS\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-495180-version-information-7\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-495180-version-information-7\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eVersion Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003e버전: 0.53.0\u003cbr\u003e\n릴리스 트랙: stable\u003cbr\u003e\nOS: darwin\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-495180-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-8\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-495180-for-ai-issues-which-model-did-you-use-8\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: which model did you use?\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAuto\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe issue occurs while Grok Bot / Builder is attempting to launch a delegated Cursor Cloud Agent. The failure occurs at Cloud Agent launch with ResourceExhausted, rather than during model inference inside the task.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-495180-for-ai-issues-add-request-id-with-privacy-disabled-9\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-495180-for-ai-issues-add-request-id-with-privacy-disabled-9\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eFor AI issues: add Request ID with privacy disabled\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eNo bc-… Background Agent ID was created because the Cloud Agent failed during launch.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eLatest Caller ID:\u003cbr\u003e\njqftxh24a9mn90ceno1y\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eError:\u003cbr\u003e\nResourceExhausted — vttablet transaction pool connection limit exceeded\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-495180-additional-information-10\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-495180-additional-information-10\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eAdditional Information\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI am filing this as a separate bug report following a suggestion from Cursor Community Support Engineer Colin in my previous Grok Bot thread.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis does not appear to be normal plan usage exhaustion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCurrent plan:\u003cbr\u003e\nCursor Ultra — $200/month\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCurrent usage at the time of the issue:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCursor Models: ~6%\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOther Models: ~1%\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGrok Bot weekly usage: ~5%\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eOn-demand spending: disabled\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe same Cloud Agent launch failure has persisted across attempts separated by many hours.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe workflow itself is not blocked by Product approval or repository state. The task is authorized and ready to execute.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThe Builder reports:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eno SHA/build produced\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003erepository unchanged\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eno automatic retry loop\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eexecution blocked specifically at Cloud Agent launch\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI would particularly like to know whether the vttablet transaction pool limit is:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003col\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCursor-side infrastructure/capacity,\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003ean account/workspace concurrency or connection-pool limit,\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eor a separate Cloud Agent quota not represented in Plan \u0026amp; Usage.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ol\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf this is account/workspace-specific, please let me know whether the relevant transaction pool can be inspected or reset.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003ch3\u003e\u003ca name=\"p-495180-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-11\" class=\"anchor\" href=\"#p-495180-does-this-stop-you-from-using-cursor-11\" aria-label=\"Heading link\"\u003e\u003c/a\u003eDoes this stop you from using Cursor\u003c/h3\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSometimes - I can sometimes use Cursor\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":1,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-18T15:56:04.527Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":6,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":30.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":172166,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-cloud-agent-consistently-fails-with-resourceexhausted-vttablet-transaction-pool-connection-limit-exceeded","display_username":"Sanghoon Kang","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":2,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":138368,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-cloud-agent-consistently-fails-with-resourceexhausted-vttablet-transaction-pool-connection-limit-exceeded/172166/1","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null,"can_vote":false},{"id":495334,"name":"Sanghoon Kang","username":"Sanghoon_Kang","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/sanghoon_kang/{size}/121272_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-18T16:35:41.909Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eUpdate: the issue has now recovered without any account or plan changes.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eAfter the ResourceExhausted / vttablet transaction pool error persisted across multiple attempts for roughly a day, I retried the exact same authorized Grok Bot → Builder → Cloud Agent workflow today.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThis time the Cloud Agent launched successfully and the workflow completed end-to-end:\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCloud Agent launch: SUCCESS\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eImplementation completed\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eCommit/push completed\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eIndependent QA completed\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e49/49 independent attacks passed\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eE2E 219/219 passed\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI did not enable on-demand spending or make any additional plan/usage changes before the successful retry.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eSo the issue appears to have been transient or infrastructure/capacity-related rather than caused by exhaustion of my Ultra plan usage.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI’m leaving this report open because the ResourceExhausted condition persisted for many hours and there was no indication in the UI of whether/when the Cloud Agent transaction pool would recover.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIt would still be helpful to know what caused the vttablet transaction pool limit and whether users can distinguish this condition from account usage/quota exhaustion.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eThanks.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":5,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-18T16:35:41.909Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":3,"readers_count":2,"score":5.6,"yours":false,"topic_id":172166,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-cloud-agent-consistently-fails-with-resourceexhausted-vttablet-transaction-pool-connection-limit-exceeded","display_username":"Sanghoon Kang","primary_group_name":null,"flair_name":null,"flair_url":null,"flair_bg_color":null,"flair_color":null,"flair_group_id":null,"badges_granted":[],"version":1,"can_edit":false,"can_delete":false,"can_recover":false,"can_see_hidden_post":false,"can_wiki":false,"read":true,"user_title":null,"bookmarked":false,"actions_summary":[],"moderator":false,"admin":false,"staff":false,"user_id":138368,"hidden":false,"trust_level":0,"deleted_at":null,"user_deleted":false,"edit_reason":null,"can_view_edit_history":false,"wiki":false,"post_url":"/t/grok-bot-cloud-agent-consistently-fails-with-resourceexhausted-vttablet-transaction-pool-connection-limit-exceeded/172166/5","reactions":[],"current_user_reaction":null,"reaction_users_count":0,"current_user_used_main_reaction":false,"can_accept_answer":false,"can_unaccept_answer":false,"accepted_answer":false,"topic_accepted_answer":null},{"id":495496,"name":"Kevin Neilson","username":"kevinn","avatar_template":"/user_avatar/forum.cursor.com/kevinn/{size}/101206_2.png","created_at":"2026-09-18T23:14:35.999Z","cooked":"\u003cp\u003eHey \u003ca class=\"mention\" href=\"/u/sanghoon_kang\"\u003e@Sanghoon_Kang\u003c/a\u003e, thanks for the report, and for the update that the same workflow completed.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eTo answer your three questions: this was a Cursor-side service degradation, not anything on your account. On Sep 17 between 15:20 and 20:04 UTC (Sep 18, 00:20 to 05:04 KST) Cloud Agents and Automations were degraded: \u003ca href=\"https://status.cursor.com/incidents/jdm0j510q78b\" class=\"inline-onebox\"\u003eCursor Status - Investigating service degradation — Cloud Agents and Automations\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eCloud Agent launches during that window were failing with that same “transaction pool connection limit exceeded” message. It is not a per-account pool, not a concurrency limit, and not a separate quota, and there is nothing on your side to inspect or reset. Your Ultra usage was never the blocker. The “Caller ID” in the message is an internal identifier, not something tied to your workspace.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI checked your account: the launch attempts on Sep 18 between 00:46 and 01:44 KST hit that window. The next launch that reached us was Sep 19 at 00:58 KST, and that one succeeded. That matches what you reported: the workflow completed without any plan or account change. Earlier “still failing” updates look like the Builder repeating its PLATFORM BLOCKED card, which says it will not launch again until a human re-hands the task.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eIf a launch fails again, reply here with the time it happened (with timezone) and the exact message, and I’ll take another look.\u003c/p\u003e","post_number":7,"post_type":1,"posts_count":3,"updated_at":"2026-09-18T23:14:35.999Z","reply_count":0,"reply_to_post_number":null,"quote_count":0,"incoming_link_count":1,"reads":2,"readers_count":1,"score":5.4,"yours":false,"topic_id":172166,"topic_slug":"grok-bot-cloud-agent-consistently-fails-with-resourceexhausted-vttablet-transaction-pool-connection-limit-exceeded","display_username":"Kevin Neilson","primary_group_name":"CursorStaff","flair_name":"CursorStaff","flair_url":"https://us1.discourse-cdn.com/cursor1/original/3X/a/d/ad08adc640929ae1e98be69dab1ad0844cee99a0.png","flair_bg_color":"","flair_color":"","flair_group